cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or code, please cite it as below."
title: "nl2sql-onprem-bench: How far do on-premises open LLMs get on Text-to-SQL? A cross-family size and technique frontier on BIRD"
abstract: >-
  Harness, per-item predictions and analysis scripts for a controlled benchmark of
  open-weight LLMs on the BIRD development split (n=1534) with a single zero-shot
  prompt, scored with the official BIRD execution-accuracy comparison (set equality)
  on read-only databases. Covers Qwen2.5-Coder-Instruct (7B, 14B, 32B) and
  CodeLlama-Instruct (7B, 13B) self-hosted at 16-bit precision, Llama-3.1-8B and
  Llama-3.3-70B through an FP8 API, and Qwen2.5-Coder-32B through OpenRouter with a
  whitespace repair for a provider output defect. Lexical and embedding schema
  linking, execution-guided self-correction and self-consistency are ablated, and
  every within-model recipe difference is tested with paired exact McNemar tests,
  Holm correction and a database-clustered bootstrap. Release 0.3.0 corrects harness
  defects of the preprint (read-write databases, multiset comparison, SQL extraction,
  embedder race), re-scores all released runs and adds the re-runs and the scripts
  that regenerate every number, table and figure of the revised paper.
